# Cloudflare Pages headers — global security + caching profile.
#
# Lighthouse audit 2026-05-16 (https://advertisehomes.online/en/properties/...)
# flagged five Best Practices items: missing CSP, weak HSTS, no COOP, no XFO,
# no Trusted Types. This file resolves all five.
#
# Pages reads _headers at deploy time and rewrites them onto every matching
# response. Patterns work left-to-right; first match wins. Wildcards * match
# a single path segment; /* matches everything from that point.
#
# Notes on the choices below:
#  - frame-ancestors 'none' + X-Frame-Options DENY — AHO listings shouldn't
#    embed in third-party iframes. Stripe Checkout opens in a popup, not an
#    iframe; Tawk widget loads cross-origin scripts (allowed via script-src)
#    but doesn't iframe us back.
#  - script-src includes the live-chat + Turnstile + Cloudflare Insights +
#    Stripe origins we actually use. 'unsafe-inline' kept because Next.js
#    runtime injects inline bootstraps; tightening to nonce-based CSP is a
#    separate larger refactor.
#  - 'strict-dynamic' would be ideal but Next.js's hashed-bootstrap pattern
#    doesn't fully support it without a custom Document override.
#  - Trusted Types is opt-in via Report-Only first — flipping to enforce
#    breaks third-party widgets that touch innerHTML. Report-Only gives us
#    visibility without breakage.
#  - HSTS preload-eligible (max-age 1y + includeSubDomains + preload).
#  - COOP same-origin lets us use SharedArrayBuffer if we ever need it
#    (not today, but harmless to enable) and prevents tab-napping attacks.

/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(self), interest-cohort=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-site
  X-DNS-Prefetch-Control: on
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' 'unsafe-eval' https://challenges.cloudflare.com https://js.stripe.com https://embed.tawk.to https://*.tawk.to https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://*.tawk.to https://*.tawkcdn.com; img-src 'self' data: blob: https: https://*.tawk.to https://*.tawkcdn.com; font-src 'self' data: https://*.tawk.to https://*.tawkcdn.com; connect-src 'self' https://*.supabase.co wss://*.supabase.co https://lqujtquofsdsxtujvjtl.supabase.co https://api.stripe.com https://challenges.cloudflare.com https://*.tawk.to wss://*.tawk.to https://static.cloudflareinsights.com https://imagedelivery.net; frame-src 'self' https://js.stripe.com https://challenges.cloudflare.com https://*.tawk.to; frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self' https://api.stripe.com; upgrade-insecure-requests
  # Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only: require-trusted-types-for 'script'; trusted-types default
  # ^ Removed 2026-05-16. The Report-Only Trusted Types directive was firing console noise from
  # embedded 3rd-party widgets (Cloudflare Turnstile, Google safevalues lib) that create their
  # own internal policies (e.g. 'goog#html') we don't control. Even Report-Only logged them as
  # "blocked" in DevTools console, scaring agents. Trusted Types as a real defense requires our
  # OWN inline scripts to use TrustedHTML — Next.js's runtime emits raw inline bootstraps that
  # don't comply yet. Re-add as enforced (not Report-Only) once we wire a Trusted-Types-aware
  # nonce shim into the Document layer.

# Long-cache static asset families. Next.js builds emit hashed filenames
# under /_next/static/*, so immutable + 1y is safe.
/_next/static/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Public images / fonts — same hashed-filename guarantee from /public.
/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Service worker — never cache. Browsers handle SW cache separately; CDN
# caching of sw.js leads to "I deployed but old SW is still running" bugs.
/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache, no-store, must-revalidate

# Manifest — 1-hour cache. Small file, rarely changes, but we want quick
# propagation when icons / theme color / short_name updates land.
/manifest.webmanifest
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
